File Index

/ResetsPage.test.tsx
Purpose: Render/edit/reorder/add/remove tests proving form edits emit back into valid reset lines; mocks GET .../spawn (Phase 13) so SimulatePane's now-unconditional render doesn't hit the fetch mock's "unexpected fetch" throw.

/ResetsPage.tsx
Purpose: Resets tab — #RESETS rows in file order (order is meaning: G/E/P bind to the closest M/O above), per-command compact forms with local-entity vnum pickers, reorder/add/remove, comments read-only; Phase 12b groups each M with its G/E/P riders as a color-coded block (adjacent groups never share a color, lone rows stay plain) whose anchor moves the whole unit; 10-door labels; workbench preview/save/manual flow; renders SimulatePane (Phase 13) below the form, passing an optional initialRoomTarget prop through from App.tsx's cross-tab lift, and (2026-07-26) an onEditRoom prop straight through to SimulatePane for its reverse "Edit this room" link. 2026-07-26: the resets array/blocking/mutation logic and the per-command field JSX were extracted to reset-editing.tsx (useResetsEditor/ResetRowFields) — this file now just wires that hook + component into its own list/reorder/add UI (own ResetsPage.test.tsx suite passed unmodified, proving the extraction is behavior-preserving); addReset now takes the command explicitly (was reading local newCommand state via closure). 2026-07-26 (UX polish pass): AreaSidebar now gets onBeforeOpen={() => wb.confirmDiscard('switch areas')} (Step 5 dirty-guard rollout) — individual reset-row add/remove deliberately do NOT get success toasts (too fine-grained/high-frequency, per the plan's own stated reasoning).

/reset-editing.tsx
Purpose: Extracted from ResetsPage.tsx for reuse by the Areas dashboard's accordions (features/areas/MobPlacementAccordion.tsx, ObjectPlacementAccordion.tsx) — the SAME Reset rows a room's mob/object accordion edits are these rows, not a copy. Exports: entityOptions/VnumField/NumArg (vnum pickers with local-entity suggestions), GROUP_COLORS/ResetBlock/computeBlocks (M+trailing G/E/P riders = one movable block), COMMAND_NAMES/DOOR_LABELS/DOOR_STATES, useResetsEditor(wb) (resets array + blocks + update/move/moveBlock/remove/addReset(command) over a shared AreaWorkbench), ResetRowFields (the per-command field JSX, parameterized by an onChange(patch) callback rather than a closure-bound index so callers control where the edit lands), and (2026-07-26) contentsOf(resets, oIndex) — the contiguous run of `P` rows filling one specific `O` placement (arg3 matches that O's arg1 object vnum; NOT part of computeBlocks, which only groups M+G/E/P), used by ObjectPlacementAccordion's "Contents" sub-accordion.

/SimulatePane.test.tsx
Purpose: Mocked-fetch tests: gear-tree rendering (equipped slot label + nested P contents inside carried objects), warnings shown above the room list, boot-state disclaimer always present, room filter by vnum/name, initialRoomTarget seeds the filter and auto-opens the single match, fetch-error state (no crash), Refresh re-fetches. Phase 14c: "Compare live" polls (fake timers) to a fresh snapshot and renders per-room drift (anchored on vnum since two rooms can render an identical "expected 1, live 0" line), and shows a "did not respond" note instead of hanging when the game never produces one within the ~10s bound. 2026-07-26: "Edit this room" fires onEditRoom with (vnum, file) scoped to the correct room (two rooms rendered, asserted via `within`); no link at all when onEditRoom isn't provided.

/SimulatePane.tsx
Purpose: Renders GET /api/areas/:file/spawn (Phase 13, merc-area's simulateResets) as a per-room <details> accordion — mobs with gear trees (equipped + carried, recursive P contents), room objects, door states, randomized-exit rooms — merging the API's separate rooms/doors/randomizedExits lists into one per-room view client-side; warnings up top, a boot-state disclaimer, a room filter (vnum or resolved room name), a Refresh button, and an optional initialRoomTarget prop for the Rooms tab's RoomEditor cross-tab hand-off. Strictly a VIEW over the on-disk saved file, same convention as World/Map — does not reflect unsaved edits above. Phase 14c: a "Compare live" button POSTs /api/state/refresh then polls GET /api/state/live (1s interval, ~10s bound) for a snapshot newer than whatever was already on record; the WORLD-WIDE snapshot is filtered down to this area's own room vnums (from the `area` prop) BEFORE diffing — required, not cosmetic: a live E2E deploy check caught 111 cross-area rooms surfacing as false "extra" drift before this filter existed. Diffs via merc-area's diffSpawnState and renders missing mobs/extra+missing objects/live player counts/door drift per room (mob/object vnums resolved to names from the `area` prop, since the live snapshot itself is vnum-only) plus a summary header; drift clears on area change; a timeout shows a plain "did not respond" note rather than hanging. 2026-07-26: an optional onEditRoom(vnum, file) prop renders a reverse "Edit this room →" link in each room's <summary> (stopPropagation'd — it lives inside a <details>/<summary>, a plain click would also toggle the native disclosure) — the completing half of RoomEditor's existing "See what spawns here" link, landing back on the Rooms tab.
